Check out the PR head. Run every command from the repo root and compare output byte for byte. A good way is to pipe it into `od -c`, or compare against a file made with printf. `npm install` is not needed; there are no dependencies.

Check 1. Expect: `printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv` prints exactly `[{"a":"1","b":"2"}]` followed by a newline and exits 0.
Run: `printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv > /tmp/o1; echo "exit=$?"; printf '[{"a":"1","b":"2"}]\n' | cmp - /tmp/o1 && echo SAME`.
PASS: exit=0 and SAME. FAIL: any other exit code, or the output differs.

Check 2. Expect: With --tsv, commas inside a field stay literal: `printf 'name\tnote\nx\thello, world\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv` prints exactly `[{"name":"x","note":"hello, world"}]` followed by a newline.
Run: `printf 'name\tnote\nx\thello, world\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv > /tmp/o2; printf '[{"name":"x","note":"hello, world"}]\n' | cmp - /tmp/o2 && echo SAME`.
PASS: SAME. FAIL: the output differs.

Check 3. Expect: With --tsv and several data rows, every row comes out in order: `printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n3\t4\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv` prints exactly `[{"a":"1","b":"2"},{"a":"3","b":"4"}]` followed by a newline.
Run: `printf 'a\tb\n1\t2\n3\t4\n' | node bin/csv2json.js --tsv > /tmp/o3; printf '[{"a":"1","b":"2"},{"a":"3","b":"4"}]\n' | cmp - /tmp/o3 && echo SAME`.
PASS: SAME. FAIL: the output differs.

